{"availability":"available","full":"kindintelligence/dioxus-dnd","name":"dioxus-dnd","description":"Modular, accessible drag-and-drop for Dioxus","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":9,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-05T02:49:46Z","updated":"2026-09-02T08:52:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kindintelligence.github.io/dioxus-dnd/","topics":[],"demo":"https://kindintelligence.github.io/dioxus-dnd/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T09:02:18.056Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T09:02:18.056Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T09:02:18.056Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T09:02:18.056Z","stars":9,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The chart never stops streaming - even inside the drag ghost, mid-flight between windows. Multi-window desktop drags carry live Rust values: the payload above holds a live Signal handle, something no serialized OS drag protocol could move. Ctrl-drop clones a running widget; windows close in any order mid-drag. That's examples/desktop-showcase/, built entirely on the public API.","Pick it up. Put it anywhere. Modular, accessible drag and drop for Dioxus: one small core, one module per drop pattern, use only what you need. Keyboard accessible by default, touch-ready out of the box, live drop previews, and auto-scroll. The library ships no JavaScript of its own: everything is Rust, and the optional web feature reaches browser pointer capture through web-sys bindings.","value through Dioxus context. No DataTransfer string round-trips, no JSON, no ids-as-strings."],"features":["Typed payloads, no serialization. In-app drags carry any Clone Rust","One input model. Pointer events serve mouse, touch and pen; keyboard","Native where it must be. OS file drops, native file-picker selections,","Headless and Tailwind-ready. No CSS ships. Drag state is exposed as","Accessible by default. Space picks up, arrows navigate zones"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.